{
  "title": "Palindrome Fence Fewest Cuts",
  "description": "## Task\n\nA fence is painted in a row of colours given as a string, one letter per panel. The owner wants to saw the fence into consecutive sections so that every section reads the same forwards and backwards. Find the smallest number of saw cuts needed.\n\n## Input\n\n- `paint` — a string of lowercase letters. It may be empty.\n\n## Output\n\nThe minimum number of cuts so that every resulting piece is a palindrome. A string that is already a palindrome (or empty) needs 0.\n\n## Example\n\n```python\nfewest_fence_cuts(\"aab\")  # returns 1\nfewest_fence_cuts(\"abcba\")  # returns 0\nfewest_fence_cuts(\"abcd\")  # returns 3\n```\n\n## Constraints\n\n- 0 ≤ length of `paint` ≤ 2000\n- Only lowercase letters a–z.\n",
  "signature": "def fewest_fence_cuts(paint: str) -> int",
  "topic": "palindrome partition",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "category": "dynamic-programming",
  "tests": [
    { "args": ["aab"], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": ["abcba"], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": ["abcd"], "expected": 3 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": ["a"], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": ["aaaa"], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": ["abacabadabacaba"], "expected": 0 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 1 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 1499 },
    { "args": [""], "expected": 1 }
  ]
